eading"},{"kind":"list","text":"Study of music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Poetry, both reading, analyzing, and writing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Exploring where you live or where you're from"},{"kind":"list","text":"Talking to relatives about your ancestors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Daydreaming"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sipping tea"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ballet/modern dance"},{"kind":"list","text":"Riding a bike"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shopping"},{"kind":"list","text":"Baths"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Literature"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pride and Prejudice by Jane Austen (1813)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sense and Sensibility by Jane Austen (1811)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Emma by Jane Austen (1815)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Women by Louisa May Alcott (1868)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Orlando: A Biography by Virginia Woolf (1928)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Importance of Being Earnest by Oscar Wilde (1895)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Picture of Dorian Gray by Oscar Wilde (1890)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Romeo and Juliet by William Shakespeare (1597)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sally Potter’s Orlando (1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sleeping Beauty (1959)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Romeo and Juliet (1968)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Romeo and Juliet (2013)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Emma (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bright Star (2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Much Ado About Nothing (1993)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chéri (2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Farewell, My Queen (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Russian Ark (2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Wings of the Dove (1997)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marie Antoinette (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Anna Karenina (2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pride and Prejudice (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Women (2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Breakfast at Tiffany’s (1961)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beauty and the Beast (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harry Potter Series (2001-2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cinderella (1950)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Plays/Ballets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Romeo and Juliet"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cyrano de Bergerac (Roland Petit)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Afternoon of A Faun (Jerome Robbins)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sleeping Beauty"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swan Lake"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"There is no specific genre, but there is certainly a heavy influence from the softer side of post-punk, baroque pop, dream pop, and shoegaze. (Sometimes even Synthpop.)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Genres"},{"kind":"list","text":"Classical"},{"kind":"list","text":"Baroque Pop"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jazz"},{"kind":"list","text":"Alternative"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ballet Soundtracks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ethereal Wave"},{"kind":"list","text":"Folk"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dream Pop"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ambient"},{"kind":"list","text":"Adult Standards"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Smiths"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Sundays"},{"kind":"list","text":"Felt"},{"kind":"list","text":"Virginia Astley"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dif Juz"},{"kind":"list","text":"This Mortal Coil"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cocteau Twins"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Dream Academy"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Ocean Blue"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shelleyan Orphan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jimmy Somerville (specifically the Orlando soundtrack)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jeff Buckley"},{"kind":"list","text":"Burt Bacharach"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lana Del Rey"},{"kind":"list","text":"Enigma"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sufjan Stevens"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hozier"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fleetwood Mac"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Velvet Underground"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Beatles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Florence and The Machine"},{"kind":"list","text":"Isak Danielson"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pink Floyd"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bob Dylan"},{"kind":"list","text":"D